      ],
      "note": "TEN of the graph's 44 `mapToolResultToToolResultBlockParam` methods are excised and delegated to reforge-owned modules (Write, Glob, TaskCreate from M3-B; Read, Edit, Bash, Grep, TaskGet, TaskList, TaskUpdate from C4/W1), 6,568 minified chars. Every one of the ten owned MODULES is standalone-complete and registered in engine-ts/modules/index.ts: it ships its own constants and pure helpers, and only typed ports cross the adapter (Read's WeakMap+clock staleness prefix and tab-separator gate, Bash's background output path and task-ack envelope/ending, TaskUpdate's two agent-team predicates). The SUBSYSTEM row nevertheless stays `spliced`, not `standalone-complete`: 34 formatters remain, so the family is not owned. Coverage is honest too — the corpus renders one of Read's six result arms, one of Grep's three and the plain stdout path of Bash's six, and never truncates a Glob result; the arms it cannot reach are graded by strangle/contracts.test.ts (135 checks). DEPENDENCY EDGES (§2.4), one per effectful-port capture that leaves this row: `tool/Read` — the Read formatter's staleness prefix is a module WeakMap keyed by the result object and populated inside the Read tool's CALL path, then rendered through a Date.now()-derived day count, so it is a side channel owned by Read's execution, not data this wave can own; `subsystem/bash-executor` — the Bash formatter's background output path reads the live outputPathBindings registry, and its task-ack envelope/ending reach the background-task machinery §1.1 files under the Bash executor; `subsystem/subagent-dispatch` — TaskUpdate's completion nudge is gated on the session's agent/team identity. Read's tab-separator capture is a feature gate, and gates are neither spliced nor excluded (§3.3), so it is a port with no edge."
    },
    {
      "id": "subsystem/tool-result-validators",
      "kind": "subsystem",
      "title": "Tool-result validators (Edit's validateInput and its 19 siblings)",
      "wave": "C4",
      "state": "unowned",
      "edges": [],
      "footprint": null,
      "note": "Split out of §1.1's 'formatters + validators' row by C4 with measured evidence: the Edit tool's error results (\"String to replace not found in file.\", \"File has not been read yet.\", the stale-read and match-count messages) are NOT produced by `mapToolResultToToolResultBlockParam`. They are returned by a sibling `async validateInput`, 3,317 minified chars against the formatters' 155-1,590, carrying filesystem reads, readFileState access, `tengu_edit_tool_stale_read` telemetry and gate reads — mostly `effectful-port` captures. It needs its own scenario (a deliberately missing `old_string`) and its own gate row, so C4 scoped it out rather than smuggling it in behind a formatter wave. 20 `validateInput` methods exist in chunk-fy12d89p.js. OPEN: this row is filed under C4 because that is the child that subdivided it, and C4 does not close it — the roadmap owes it a wave assignment (campaign spec Revision Notes, 2026-09-01)."
    },
